===Etymology 1===
From {{etyl|enm|en}} {{term|hight||tr=alternative past participle of {{term|hoten|lang=enm}}|to be named, be called|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang|en}} {{term|hēht||tr=preterite of {{m|ang|hātan}}|to be named, be called|lang=ang}}, from *''hehait-'', reduplicate preterite base of {{etyl|gem-pro|en}} {{m|gem-pro|*haitaną||to call, command, summon}}, from {{etyl|ine-pro|en}} {{m|ine-pro|*key(w)-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*kyew-||to set in motion}}. Cognate with {{etyl|nds|-}} {{term|heten|lang=nds}}, {{etyl|de|-}} {{term|heißen|lang=de}}, {{etyl|da|-}} {{term|hedde|lang=da}}, {{etyl|nl|-}} {{term|heten|lang=nl}}, and {{etyl|sv|-}} {{term|heta|lang=sv}}, {{etyl|la|-}} {{m|la|cieō||I call, I set in motion}}.

